{"display_name":"Rohit M","role":"admin"}

### Response 4
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{"id":8812,"display_name":"Rohit M","role":"admin","updated_at":"2026-11-19T11:42:08Z"}

### Request 5
GET /api/v1/invoices/4472 HTTP/1.1
Host: billing.northfield.co.in
Accept: application/json

### Response 5
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{"id":4472,"account_id":9043,"customer":"Sunita Rao","amount":"226500.00","status":"unpaid"}', 1711);
DELETE FROM lab_tasks WHERE lab_id = 'lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment';
INSERT INTO lab_tasks (id, lab_id, position, prompt, model_answer) VALUES ('lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment_t1', 'lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment', 1, 'Requests 1 and 2 are the finding. State it precisely enough for a developer to act on.', 'GET /api/v2/invoices/{id} returns any invoice to any authenticated caller. The same bearer token for account 8812 returns invoice 4471 belonging to account 8812 and invoice 4472 belonging to account 9043. The endpoint authenticates the caller but never checks that the invoice belongs to them. Broken object-level authorisation, and the fix is an ownership check on the record, not on the route.');
INSERT INTO lab_tasks (id, lab_id, position, prompt, model_answer) VALUES ('lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment_t2', 'lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment', 2, 'Request 3 returns 403. Why does that make the finding stronger rather than weaker?', 'Because it proves the application knows how to do this. /api/v2/accounts/9043 correctly refuses with account_scope_mismatch, so the authorisation model exists and was simply not applied to the invoices endpoint. That removes the "we never designed for this" defence and turns it from an architecture discussion into a missed check on one route, which is both more embarrassing and much easier to fix.');
INSERT INTO lab_tasks (id, lab_id, position, prompt, model_answer) VALUES ('lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment_t3', 'lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment', 3, 'Request 4 is a second, different vulnerability. Name it and say what it costs.', 'Mass assignment. The PATCH to the caller''s own account sends a role field, which a client should never be able to set, and the response confirms role is now admin. Self-service privilege escalation from a normal account. Rate it above the invoice read: one discloses data, this one makes the attacker an administrator.');
INSERT INTO lab_tasks (id, lab_id, position, prompt, model_answer) VALUES ('lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment_t4', 'lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment', 4, 'Request 5 drops the Authorization header entirely and still returns data. What have you actually found?', 'An old API version left routable with no authentication at all. /api/v1/invoices/4472 returns the record unauthenticated, which means the v2 access control conversation is beside the point while v1 is reachable. Retired versions that were never actually retired are one of the most common ways a well-secured API leaks, and nobody is monitoring them because nobody remembers they exist.');
INSERT INTO lab_tasks (id, lab_id, position, prompt, model_answer) VALUES ('lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment_t5', 'lab_pentest_idor-and-mass-assignment', 5, 'How do you order these three in the report, and what do you say about remediation sequence?', 'Unauthenticated v1 first, because it needs no account at all. Mass assignment second, because it gives an attacker admin. Invoice object access third. On sequence, say that fixing v2 while v1 is still routable fixes nothing, so turning off v1 is the immediate action and the authorisation work follows. Giving a remediation order rather than a severity list is what makes a report usable.');

INSERT OR REPLACE INTO labs (id, title, role, level, brief, artifact_kind, artifact_name, is_free, difficulty, created_at) VALUES ('lab_cloud_leaked-key-in-the-trail', 'The deploy key woke up in another country', 'cloud', 'mid', 'Control-plane audit events from one cloud account for a single day, pulled after the billing alert showed data transfer out of a region you do not use. The deploy pipeline is supposed to be the only thing using automation credentials here.', 'table', 'audit-trail-1119.csv', 0, 2, '2026-11-22T07:15:26.590Z');
